%% C2 - Container Diagram | SocialU | Planned semester architecture
%% Authors: left blank for the team to assign.
%% This diagram follows the professor's Container View structure.
%% C1 SocialU is opened into Web App and Backend API; Supabase and Resend stay external.
%% Backend API is exactly the container expanded by docs/architecture/c3.mmd.
%% The browser client and server API share one Next.js project, not separate microservices.
%% Web App means the React browser runtime, with pages/assets served by Next.js.
%% The server hosting provider is not selected; no Vercel or other host is invented.
%% Supabase is the hosted-cloud provider, grouping Database, Auth, Storage and Realtime.
%% The manually arranged c2.svg/c2.png and this Mermaid source use the same eight nodes
%% and nine relationships. Mermaid may arrange the same model differently.
%% Single arrows show uses/dependencies; responses are implicit. The double arrow
%% denotes the persistent bidirectional WebSocket connection (subscriptions / updates).
%% Student is the single top-level user class, matching C1 and the approved URD.
%% Web App owns screens, navigation, avatar preview and browser gameplay movement,
%% jumping, collisions, pause and unsaved attempt state (UR-600 to UR-627).
%% Backend API owns account/authorization rules, feature operations and confirmed saves.
%% C3 provides the eleven internal API components; they are intentionally not shown here.
%% Durable data includes the single SS participation record consumed by DP points,
%% never a second independent reward streak (SRS-613.13; UR-526).
%% Database contains 59 tables in the socialu schema; no schema change is proposed.
%% Source schema SHA-256: cfadaa90ee900e61591aec091f0f707acc9a47610d0cccaa6502608e7cc58d65.
%% Database calls use Supabase REST/RPC over HTTPS; SQL transactions run in PostgreSQL.
%% Storage contains private photographs. The API checks owner, audience, membership
%% and Snipe consent/removal before allowing media access; this is planned behavior.
%% Supabase Auth is already used by the starter. Mapping the provider to students,
%% authentication_challenges and login_sessions in the new schema remains open.
%% The Web App calls the API with HTTPS JSON and an access token for protected requests;
%% it is not granted unrestricted database access by this proposed architecture.
%% User-requested revision: show WebSocket transport for the existing chat feature.
%% Proposed transport: Supabase Realtime Broadcast, not a new standalone socket server.
%% Supports UR-201 (message delivery/display), UR-202 to UR-208 (group chat), and
%% UR-213 (privacy), especially SRS-213.6 (former members receive no new messages).
%% Browser chat sends still go through Backend API HTTPS operations. Only committed,
%% authorized chat updates are published through the Realtime HTTPS Broadcast API.
%% The Web App subscribes using WSS (secure WebSocket), with an authenticated token.
%% Use private recipient channels; the server rechecks current membership/visibility
%% when selecting recipients for each publication, including blocks and Snipe consent.
%% Joining a conversation channel once must not grant indefinite future access.
%% Live events do not replace durable message history; the API reloads permitted
%% history after reconnecting. No typing indicators or presence feature is invented.
%% Realtime identity mapping and private-channel authorization remain to implement;
%% this drawing is not evidence of configured policies or functioning live chat.
%% No changes to database/schema.sql are made by this transport design.
%% C3 keeps the same eleven components; its Chat & Snipes component will need the
%% corresponding Realtime publish dependency added during the next C3 review.
%% Transport reference: https://supabase.com/docs/guides/realtime/broadcast
%% Authorization reference: https://supabase.com/docs/guides/realtime/authorization
%% Resend is proposed, not configured. SocialU owns verification validity/account rules;
%% Resend delivers verification, password-reset and security emails (SRS-101.2,
%% SRS-102.2, SRS-103.7, SRS-104.2, SRS-105.16, SRS-106.6).
%% Game 1 has three required levels; the fourth and Wordle are optional.
%% Wordle exposes only today. Snipes remain in their original conversation.
%% Events and Trending share one page. Drafts and university transfers are deferred.
%% No instructor, LLM provider, socket server, scheduler, native app or payment service
%% is added from the professor's example; none is an agreed SocialU C1 dependency.
%% Sources: documentation/SocialU_SRS_Editable.md, documentation/user_requirements.md,
%% database/schema.sql and database/schema_review.md.
flowchart LR
    Student["Student<br/>[Person]<br/>Student at the<br/>launch university."]

    subgraph SocialU["SocialU [software system]"]
        direction LR
        WebApp["Web App<br/>[Next.js / React / TypeScript]<br/>Runs in the student browser.<br/>Screens and live chat;<br/>avatar and gameplay;<br/>client attempt / pause state."]
        BackendAPI["Backend API<br/>[Next.js Route Handlers / TypeScript]<br/>Runs on the application server.<br/>Account and access rules;<br/>chat and other features;<br/>authorize and save."]
    end

    subgraph Supabase["Supabase [hosted cloud; external system]"]
        direction TB
        Realtime["Supabase Realtime<br/>[WebSocket; proposed]<br/>Private / group chat updates."]
        Database[("Supabase Database<br/>[PostgreSQL]<br/>59 tables in socialu;<br/>SQL transactions.")]
        Auth["Supabase Auth<br/>[External service]<br/>Identity / sessions;<br/>accounts and tokens."]
        Storage["Supabase Storage<br/>[External service]<br/>Private photographs."]
    end

    Resend["Resend<br/>[External system; proposed]<br/>Delivers account emails."]

    Student -->|"Uses<br/>SocialU"| WebApp
    WebApp -->|"Calls API<br/>HTTPS / JSON + access token"| BackendAPI
    WebApp <-->|"Live private / group chat<br/>WSS / WebSocket"| Realtime
    BackendAPI -->|"Publishes chat updates<br/>HTTPS / Broadcast"| Realtime
    BackendAPI -->|"Reads / writes<br/>HTTPS · REST/RPC"| Database
    BackendAPI -->|"Identity / sessions<br/>HTTPS / Auth API"| Auth
    BackendAPI -->|"Private photographs<br/>HTTPS / Storage API"| Storage
    BackendAPI -->|"Requests account emails<br/>HTTPS / email API"| Resend
    Resend -->|"Delivers account emails"| Student

    classDef person fill:#173f52,stroke:#173f52,color:#ffffff,stroke-width:2px;
    classDef container fill:#e3f0e8,stroke:#31735b,color:#163743,stroke-width:3px;
    classDef external fill:#f0f3f5,stroke:#6e7f89,color:#163743,stroke-width:2px,stroke-dasharray:8 5;
    class Student person;
    class WebApp,BackendAPI container;
    class Database,Auth,Storage,Realtime,Resend external;
    style SocialU fill:#ffffff,stroke:#31735b,stroke-width:3px
    style Supabase fill:#ffffff,stroke:#6e7f89,stroke-width:2px,stroke-dasharray:8 5
    linkStyle default stroke:#395664,stroke-width:2.5px;
